v1.1:
  - gitHubInfo in the "user:branch" format SetupHelper expects (was "user/repo:branch":
    a copy installed by hand in /data was added to PackageManager with a wrong GitHub user)
  - Command line hints and help name the command as typed: victron-ble (was cli.py)

v1.0:
  - Initial release
  - Victron Bluetooth Instant Readout devices published as read-only Venus OS D-Bus services:
      DC/DC converters (Orion-Tr Smart, Orion Smart) -> com.victronenergy.dcdc.ble_<mac>
      AC chargers (Blue Smart IP22/IP65/IP67, Phoenix Smart) -> com.victronenergy.charger.ble_<mac>
  - Passive listening on the Linux HCI monitor channel (no GATT, no pairing, no btmon process)
  - Scan by the Venus OS Bluetooth sensors (turned on at the first installation only); own BlueZ
    discovery when the user turns them off, stopped when they come back on
  - Whitelist /data/conf/victron-ble.json (MAC + key), hot reload, atomic writes
  - Stable VRM instance through localsettings ClassAndVrmInstance; /Connected = 0 after timeout_s
  - Name editable from the GUI / VRM, saved in the whitelist
  - Devices already on D-Bus (VE.Direct...) are not published twice unless "allow_duplicate"
  - Command line victron-ble: discover, add, remove, validate, decode
  - AES-128: python3-cryptography, else OpenSSL libcrypto through ctypes, else pure Python
  - Parsers derived from victron_ble 0.9.3 (Unlicense)
  - Tested on Venus OS v3.75, Raspberry Pi 5: Orion-Tr Smart 12/12-18, Blue Smart IP65 12|25
